      "writtenOn": "2019-10-31T17:43:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "About changing the name to board_get_src_dts_polarity(), this has a different meaning, that  the caller explicitly knows the port is SRC DTS and calls this board function for the predetermined polarity. It is like:\n\nif (new_cc_state \u003d\u003d PD_CC_UFP_DEBUG_ACC)\n    pd[port].polarity \u003d board_get_src_dts_polarity();\nelse\n    pd[port].polarity \u003d (cc1 !\u003d TYPEC_CC_VOLT_RD);\n\n\nAnd the above soft reset case, can do the same thing, just adding some check for the PD_CC_UFP_DEBUG_ACC.\n\nI think this is better for spec compliance. What do you think?",
